    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'development' is very broad, encompassing growth, progress, creation, and exploitation across various domains. While 開拓 (kaitaku) can mean 'development' in the specific sense of 'reclamation (e.g. of wasteland)' or 'pioneering/opening up (e.g. of a new market)', it is too narrow for the general 'development' concept. For common English uses like 'economic development', 'software development', or 'child development', Japanese would typically use 開発 (kaihatsu), 発展 (hatten), or 発達 (hattatsu) respectively. 開拓 is not the most natural or standard term a general learner would expect for the core concept of 'development'.",
